 "_doc": "Pose library for the stick-figure rig (see rig.json for conventions). Each pose sets lean (torso angle from vertical, + = forward), head (extra head tilt on top of the lean), hip ([dx, dy] offset from the default hip; +dy lowers the hips), and limbs as [upper_angle, lower_bend]: aF/aN = far/near arm, lF/lN = far/near leg. Missing fields fall back to 'stand'. 'loop' poses are meant to be combined with the walk/run cycle. Use the action expansions in actions.json for repeated motions (wave, scrub, stomp, nod, laugh, shiver). 'turn' (0-1, default 0, never inherited from stand) switches between the side-view stance (both arms from one shoulder) and the front-view stance of the reference videos (arms from the left and right shoulders); front poses use mirrored angles (far limbs negative = to the -x side, near limbs positive). fFront 1 = draw the far (back) arm in front of the body, for arms that cross or meet in front of the chest.",
